             handed on to MainActivity in the application's own task: a messenger starts a view for a result, which
             would stack MainActivity inside the messenger's task. Nothing but these files is routed here: a recipe file
             by the product's own type, whatever the address; either by its extension, whatever type the sender
             declares or none. -->
        <activity
            android:name=".file.OpenRecipeFileActivity"
            android:excludeFromRecents="true"
            android:exported="true"
            android:noHistory="true"
            android:taskAffinity=""
            android:theme="@android:style/Theme.NoDisplay">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
                <data android:scheme="content" />
                <data android:scheme="file" />
                <data android:mimeType="application/vnd.recipefork.recipe+zip" />
            </intent-filter>
            <!-- A messenger declares what type it likes (Telegram: the stored one, else text/plain), so the extension is
                 taken with any type, and with none. A path pattern does not backtrack: each `.*\\.` stops at the next
                 dot, so a path holding N dots — in its folders or its name — needs the pattern with N of them. A path
                 pattern minds case: the extension is taken in lower case and in upper case. -->
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
                <data android:scheme="content" />
                <data android:scheme="file" />
                <data android:host="*" />
                <data android:mimeType="*/*" />
                <data android:pathPattern=".*\\.recipefork" />
